tools
# The citation-anchor guard must survive a fresh clone, or the rot it prevents simply
# recurs. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so `tools` has
# to be re-admitted first and its contents excluded again — a bare
# `!SentinelQuesting/tools/check_citation_anchors.py` here looks right and does nothing.
!SentinelQuesting/tools/
SentinelQuesting/tools/*
!SentinelQuesting/tools/check_citation_anchors.py
# `shared/src/zone.rs::ZONE_TABLE` is generated and checked in as source. The generator has to
# ship with it: a table nobody can regenerate is a table nobody can audit, and the module doc
# points straight at this path.
!SentinelQuesting/tools/gen_zone_table.py
# `sentinel/tests/fixtures/spell_chain_tbc243.lua` is generated from tbcmangos.sqlite and checked
# in as the offline suite's only view of the game database — the database itself is 298 MB and
# gitignored below, so CI can never re-derive it. Same rule as the two above: a fixture nobody can
# regenerate is a fixture nobody can audit, and `--check` is the only thing that catches it
# drifting from the database. Re-admit the directory before the file, per the note above.
!sentinel/tools/
sentinel/tools/*
!sentinel/tools/*
# (whole directory: these are curated, committed provenance tools — the generated catalogs are
# only auditable if their generators ship beside them, and a per-file re-admit list here is how
# the taxi-node generator got silently swallowed by the bare `tools` rule.)
OLD*
StrathDuoMage*
_scripts
_dev
Database/
Database/

